  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">East Zarqa Wastewater Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Bank signed a loan up to USD 20 million to the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan  on 17 Dec 2015.  The construction of a new wastewater pipeline from East Zarqa pumping station  to As-Samra Wastewater Treatment Plant (&apos;As-Samra WWTP&apos;). As-Samra WWTP,  Jordan&apos;s largest wastewater treatment plant, has been placed under  unprecedented strain due to the rapidly increasing wastewater flows caused by  the recent refugee influx. The proposed investment is part of a wider engagement with the Water Authority  of Jordan aimed at upgrading Jordanis wastewater system.</narrative>
  </description>
